## Context

Project pages 27 (ZAF 16, SEN 5, IDN 3, VNM 3), official news 11 and secondary
news 2. Lowest yield per document and the highest risk of over-reading: news is
an attributed statement, not evidence of delivery, and a project page is
usually already reached through a `refers_to` row from [[0875]]'s tables. These
are extracted as lines attached to existing identities, so a page that names no
known project mints nothing.

## Work

- Extract lines with LLM-assisted reading and row-by-row diff review; a
  publisher page repeated across projects gets one parser.
- Keep statements attributed to their speaker; classification and axis follow
  the ontology's status axes. Secondary news never supports a delivery status.
- Cross-check each page against the 315 `project-source-links` already held;
  a page already justifying a link gains its lines without a new referent.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Each of the 40 (after 1501) has lines or a recorded disposition
- [ ] No page mints a project, asset or agreement by itself; new identities, if any, come by the matching tiers of `docs/jetp-fusion.md` § 3
- [ ] Lines of previously extracted documents are byte-identical
- [ ] `make jetp-ledger-check`, `make check-fast` and `make lint` pass
